# 157. CRITICAL RESTRICTIONS

DO NOT:

* rebuild Phases 1–13
* delete existing functionality
* replace working architecture without justification
* expose PostgreSQL publicly by default
* expose Redis publicly
* commit `.env`
* commit secrets
* commit production data
* commit employee data
* commit database dumps containing real data
* hardcode cloud credentials
* hardcode domain names
* hardcode API keys
* hardcode production passwords
* disable authentication
* disable RBAC
* bypass tenant isolation
* expose AI direct database access
* execute arbitrary AI-generated SQL
* automatically destroy databases
* use destructive migrations casually
* deploy untested code
* deploy if CI fails
* silently ignore migration errors
* use insecure default credentials in production
* introduce Kubernetes unnecessarily for the initial DEV environment

